<section class="py-10 sm:py-14 bg-page min-h-screen">
  <div class="gutter max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <div class="card-surface legal-hero">
      <span class="legal-hero__eyebrow">privacy</span>
      <h1 class="title mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-secondary text-sm mb-0">How FindIt collects, uses, and protects your information.</p>
      <p class="text-xs text-muted-custom mt-3 mb-0">Last updated: <%= updatedAt %></p>
    </div>

    <div class="card-surface legal-body">
      <h2>1. information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>account information (name, email, profile image if provided)</li>
        <li>report data (item details, category, location, timestamps)</li>
        <li>contact request messages and verification responses</li>
        <li>technical and security logs (IP, device/session metadata)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. how we use your information</h2>
      <p>
        We use collected data to operate the platform, match lost/found reports, support claim verification, prevent
        abuse, and improve reliability and security.
      </p>

      <h2>3. contact visibility and sharing</h2>
      <p>
        Contact details are limited and shared only as needed within approved recovery workflows. We do not publish
        private contact information publicly by default.
      </p>

      <h2>4. data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain data only as necessary for legitimate operational, security, legal, and dispute-resolution purposes,
        then delete or anonymize where appropriate.
      </p>

      <h2>5. security practices</h2>
      <p>
        We apply reasonable administrative and technical safeguards. However, no online system can guarantee absolute
        security.
      </p>

      <h2>6. your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>update profile and report details from your account</li>
        <li>remove report content when no longer needed</li>
        <li>request account-related support through platform administrators</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. cookies and session storage</h2>
      <p>
        We use session mechanisms required for authentication, security, and core functionality. Disabling these may
        limit platform use.
      </p>

      <h2>8. policy updates</h2>
      <p>
        We may revise this policy from time to time. Material updates will be reflected on this page with a revised
        update date.
      </p>

      <h2>9. contact</h2>
      <p>For privacy questions or concerns, contact the platform administrators through official support channels.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .legal-hero,
  .legal-body {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
  }
  .legal-hero {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .legal-hero__eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
  }
  .legal-body h2 {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
    text-transform: capitalize;
  }
  .legal-body p,
  .legal-body li {
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .legal-body ul {
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.2rem;
  }
  .legal-body h2 + p {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .legal-body p {
    margin: 0 0 0.95rem;
  }
</style>
